*Introduction and thesis statement:*
In the poorly understood Second Intermediate Period(2IP), some of the most challenging problems centre on the 16#super[th] Dynasty. Indeed, one of the standard histories of ancient Egypt by Van De Mieroop consigns the 14#super[th] and 16#super[th] Dynasties to a few sentences noting that: "We do not know who should be counted as members of these dynasties, whose very existence is disputed" @VanDeMieroop2021[p.~131].

There are serious questions about its origin, its nature and how the transition
to the 17#super[th] Dynasty occurred.
- *Origin:*
  - Was it the rump of the decaying 13#super[th] Dynasty forced out of Memphis?
  - Did it originate independently in Thebes?
  - Did it originate in Palestine or Egypt?
- *Nature:*
  - Was it a vassal client of the Hyksos?
  - Was it a separate dynasty that strove to be independent of them?
  - Was there a separate "Abydos Dynasty"?
- *Transition to 17#super[th] Dynasty:*
  - Were there close familial connections between the 16#super[th] and 17#super[th] Dynasties that led to a seamless transition?
  - Were they different families and was there a sinificant event leading to the transition?

There are currently two main camps in the Egyptological community with respect to these questions. The older theory, proposed by Jürgen von Beckerath, is that the
16#super[th] Dynasty was from Asia and that they were vassals of the Hyksos. A newer theory,
championed by Kim Ryholt, is that the 16#super[th] Dynasty was a native Egyptian one, that it was independent of the
Hyksos and that it ruled from Thebes until it was conquered by the Hyksos, leading to the rise of the 17#super[th] Dynasty at Thebes.
Ryholt also argues that there was a small independent dynasty at Abydos during this time.
Alexander Ilin-Tomich has looked at the origin of the 16#super[th] Dynasty and whether it came out of the 13#super[th], rather than arising independently.

Provisionally, my thesis is: "This paper will argue that, although the evidence is spotty, Kim Ryholt's contention that the 16#super[th] Dynasty originated in Thebes and was not a vassal of the Hyksos is the most reasonable view."
