+ Following the thorough work of Ryhold in examining the Turin King-list
  it is the most important single source of information on the 2IP and the 16#super[th] Dynasty. (Evidence: Turin King List)

*Methodology & Evidence:* As noted above, we are not blessed with much physical
or textual evidence for the 16th Dynasty. The Turin King List, and two versions of Manetho are the
primary textual sources. We also have some seals and tomb evidence on the physical side.

Given this, taking an _Object Biography_ approach seems to be appropriate in both areas.
It will develop the context for the evidence and will also help us to determine what can and cannot
be read into the evidence.

